# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to share your .python-version.
#   For an app, this can be useful so that developers know what version to use.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if used in a windows and unix environment,
#   the dependencies might have different hashes.
#   For details see: https://pipenv.pypa.io/en/latest/advanced/#pipfile.lock-security-details
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock contains the resolved dependencies.
#   Should be committed to VCS.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock contains the resolved dependencies.
#   Should be committed to VCS.
# pdm.lock

